capability stats/mean  the arithmetic mean, exact then rounded once
  heroes  stats.mean
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  statistics.mean
  note    Go and Rust have no statistics package. Exact as Python's, with integers of any size where Python uses fractions: equal to Python's to the last bit on 600 random data sets observed, values from 10^-4 to 10^16 among them, and on the mean of 2^1023, 2^1023 and -2^1023, which a float sum overflows. A nan or both infinities answer a nan and one infinity itself, as Python's; minus zero answers zero, as Python's

capability stats/fast-mean  the mean as a sum of floats rounded once over the count
  heroes  stats.fast_mean
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  statistics.fmean
  note    equal to Python's fmean on the same 600 sets; a sum past the largest float fails `does_not_fit`, where Python raises OverflowError

capability stats/weighted-mean  the mean of values weighted by others
  heroes  stats.weighted_mean
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  statistics.fmean
  note    Python's `fmean(data, weights)`; equal to it on 600 sets. Weights summing to zero fail `invalid`

